Thanks for the report. To identify which undo stack deleted the file, could you please provide:

- the exact steps immediately before pressing Ctrl+Z, including how the file was created and whether Chat, Copilot CLI, or another extension changed it;
- which editor, view, or terminal had focus when Ctrl+Z was pressed;
- whether this reproduces on the latest VS Code build with extensions disabled; and
- whether the deleted file appears in the Recycle Bin or the Timeline/Local History view.

If possible, please include a minimal sample workspace or screen recording. This issue will automatically close after 7 days without the requested information.

Thanks for the additional context. Before we can determine whether this is a VS Code Remote-WSL defect or a WSL filesystem permission problem, could you confirm on the latest VS Code build and provide:

- exact steps that make a working workspace start failing;
- an affected file path plus its ownership and permissions;
- whether the default WSL user can read and write that same file from the WSL shell while VS Code is failing; and
- fresh Remote-WSL logs captured immediately after reproducing the error.

Please also clarify which VS Code settings are deleted by the workaround. This issue will automatically close after 7 days without the requested information.

Thanks for the report. Could you confirm whether this still occurs on the latest VS Code build and provide:

- the chat mode, selected model, prompt, and exact steps that leave the request pending;
- whether Chat responds in a local window on the same machine;
